<!--
  Thai strings.

  NEEDS A NATIVE REVIEW BEFORE RELEASE. This is a first pass written to get the
  app's Thai locale wired end to end — every string is translated and the plurals
  and format arguments are correct, but the register and tone have not been read
  by a Thai speaker, and this app's audience reads Thai first.

  Two conventions used throughout, worth keeping if the copy is rewritten:

  - No spaces between words, spaces between clauses. Thai does not word-space,
    and the English habit of doing so is the fastest way for a translation to
    read as machine output.
  - Thai has no grammatical plural, so every <plurals> here carries only an
    "other" item. That is not laziness: supplying "one" would make the two forms
    identical and imply a distinction the language does not draw.

  `app_name` is deliberately absent, so the launcher label stays "SU Club Fair"
  in both locales — it is the name of the event, not a description of it.
-->
